\begin{abstract}
The Organism-Ontology Blueprint Simulation Engine (OOBSE-v1.0) is a 
high-performance computational framework that transforms biological 
ontology structures into dynamically executable multiscale simulation 
kernels. The system integrates post-quantum cryptographic ingestion, 
hyperbolic manifold embeddings, sparse tensor graph construction, and 
symplectic Hamiltonian dynamics to model ecological and evolutionary 
interactions at scale. Empirical validation on a 16× NVIDIA H100 SXM5 
cluster demonstrates numerical stability, cryptographic resilience, 
semantic consistency, and large-scale tensor feasibility. OOBSE-v1.0 
provides a reproducible foundation for secure biological simulation 
across heterogeneous HPC environments.
\end{abstract}

\keywords{Biological Ontologies, High-Performance Computing, 
